§ `Home insurance policy — the rodents, insects, vermin and birds exclusion`

-- The isomorphism seed: an insurance exclusion, restyled from
-- `jl4/examples/ok/rodentsAndVermin.l4` (which is NOT modified) into the Blawx
-- seed conventions -- `@export`-with-prose on every decision, the WHERE helpers
-- lifted so each carries its own policy language, and an oracle comment on
-- every directive.
--
-- WHERE THE POLICY WORDS COME FROM. `ok/rodentsAndVermin.l4` carries the logic
-- but no prose at all. The prose is in the tree's OTHER copy of this rule,
-- `jl4/experiments/classic/vermin_and_rodent.l4:14`, as a single `@export`
-- sentence over the identical `Inputs` record:
--
--     We do not cover any loss or damage caused by rodents, insects, vermin, or
--     birds. However, this exclusion does not apply to: (a) loss or damage to
--     your contents caused by birds; or (b) ensuing covered loss unless any
--     other exclusion applies or where an animal causes water to escape from a
--     household appliance, swimming pool or plumbing, heating or air
--     conditioning system.
--
-- Every span below inside `"…"` is a contiguous substring of THAT sentence.
-- Anything outside the quotes is this file's own gloss and is written as such.
-- The policy carries NO clause number anywhere in the tree, so none is invented
-- here: an earlier draft of this seed labelled all five citations
-- "Exclusion 5(b)", which no source supports.
--
-- Note in particular what the three appliance/pool/plumbing inputs mean. The
-- proviso's condition is "where an ANIMAL CAUSES WATER TO ESCAPE FROM a
-- household appliance, swimming pool or plumbing, heating or air conditioning
-- system" -- it is not loss or damage TO those items. The L4 disjunction in
-- `an exclusion applies` is the policy's own "unless … or where …", one limb
-- per item, and the field names are the original's.
--
-- WHY THE PROSE RIDES ON THE `@export` LINE. `@export` and `@desc` are the SAME
-- annotation slot: `L4.Relational.Lower` reads one `annDesc` per declaration and
-- strips a leading `export` keyword off it. Writing `@export` on one line and
-- `@desc <prose>` on the next therefore keeps one and silently discards the
-- other, and the Blawx `rule_text` section comes out as the stub
-- "Definition of <name>." So every citation in this file is written as
-- `@export <prose>`, which is the form the openfisca corpus already uses
-- (`jl4/examples/openfisca/basic-income.l4:22`). Reported as a finding: a bare
-- `@desc` beside an `@export` should merge or diagnose, not vanish.
--
-- THREE DEVIATIONS FROM THE ORIGINAL, all measured on this tree:
--
--   * the four WHERE helpers are lifted to top-level decisions, so each gets a
--     `rule_text` section, a scenario-editor image and a tier-1 query;
--   * `not covered if` (which is `GIVEN x YIELD x`, an identity whose only job
--     is to make the source sentence scan) is dropped -- lowered it would be an
--     arity-2 auxiliary with no declaration block, i.e. noise in the emitted
--     ontology;
--   * the grouping is written with parentheses rather than by layout, and
--     `exclusion apply` is renamed `an exclusion applies` because Blawx
--     synthesises its NLG postfix from the mangled atom and the original would
--     read "<object> exclusion apply" in the scenario editor.
--
-- The third deviation needs its measurement recorded, because the original's
-- layout admits two readings and they disagree:
--
--     P1  animals AND NOT (contentsBirds OR (ensuing AND NOT exclusion))
--     P2  animals AND ((NOT contentsBirds) OR (ensuing AND NOT exclusion))
--
-- They differ exactly where `animals AND ensuing AND NOT exclusion` holds. Run
-- against the UNTOUCHED original, `rodents + ensuing covered loss, all else
-- FALSE` evaluates to FALSE, and `birds + contents + ensuing` likewise -- so the
-- original parses as P1, which is also the reading the policy wording intends.
-- Both rows are kept below and marked as grouping pins. Every other scenario in
-- this file agrees under both readings and so proves nothing about the grouping;
-- those two are the ones that do.
--
-- POLARITY, preserved deliberately: `insurance covered` is TRUE when the
-- exclusion BITES -- when the loss is NOT covered. The name is the original's
-- and is kept for isomorphism; a `covered` wrapper would be an interpretive step
-- the policy text does not take, and inventing one in a fidelity showcase is
-- exactly the wrong move.
--
-- EXPORT ORDER IS AUTHORING, NOT LAYOUT: exactly one `interview` test is emitted
-- per file and its goal is the FIRST `@export` in the file, so the headline
-- decision comes first. L4 is order-independent at the top level, so the forward
-- references below are fine.
--
-- The `§` title is added: the original has none, so `ruledoc_name` came out as
-- the filename (`Rodents`), which is what a Blawx reader sees at the top of the
-- document and as the first line of `rule_text`. Naming the instrument is worth
-- one line -- but it names only what the source names, which is the subject
-- matter and not a clause.
--
-- Each directive carries its L4-oracle value on the line after it, per
-- BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC R11: one copy, outside the emitted artifact.

DECLARE Inputs
  HAS
    `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any other exclusion applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a household appliance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a swimming pool` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Home insurance policy, the animal-damage exclusion: "We do not cover any loss or damage caused by rodents, insects, vermin, or birds. However, this exclusion does not apply to: (a) loss or damage to your contents caused by birds; or (b) ensuing covered loss unless any other exclusion applies or where an animal causes water to escape from a household appliance, swimming pool or plumbing, heating or air conditioning system." TRUE here means the exclusion BITES -- the loss is NOT covered.
GIVEN i IS AN Inputs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `insurance covered` IF
         `loss or damage by animals` i
     AND NOT (       `damage to contents and caused by birds` i
                 OR (`ensuing covered loss` i AND NOT `an exclusion applies` i))

@export The trigger: "We do not cover any loss or damage caused by rodents, insects, vermin, or birds."
GIVEN i IS AN Inputs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `loss or damage by animals` IF
        i's `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents`
     OR i's `Loss or Damage.caused by insects`
     OR i's `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin`
     OR i's `Loss or Damage.caused by birds`

@export Carve-out (a): "this exclusion does not apply to: (a) loss or damage to your contents caused by birds". Both limbs must hold -- contents damage by anything else, or damage by birds to anything else, is still excluded.
GIVEN i IS AN Inputs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damage to contents and caused by birds` IF
        i's `Loss or Damage.to Contents`
    AND i's `Loss or Damage.caused by birds`

@export Carve-out (b), first limb: the exclusion does not apply to "(b) ensuing covered loss", subject to the proviso that follows it.
GIVEN i IS AN Inputs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ensuing covered loss` IF
    i's `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss`

@export Carve-out (b), proviso: (b) is itself disapplied "unless any other exclusion applies or where an animal causes water to escape from a household appliance, swimming pool or plumbing, heating or air conditioning system". Each of the last three limbs is a condition about an ANIMAL CAUSING WATER TO ESCAPE from the item, not about loss or damage to the item.
GIVEN i IS AN Inputs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exclusion applies` IF
        i's `any other exclusion applies`
     OR i's `a household appliance`
     OR i's `a swimming pool`
     OR i's `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system`

-- the original file's own #EVAL, carried over: nothing happened
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- rats in the loft -- the bare exclusion
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- carve-out (a): contents damage caused by birds
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS TRUE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- (a) needs BOTH limbs -- birds, but not to Contents
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- (a) needs BOTH limbs -- Contents, but not by birds
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS TRUE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- GROUPING PIN: carve-out (b) with no other exclusion.
-- Under reading P2 this would be TRUE; the original says FALSE.
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS TRUE
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- GROUPING PIN: (a) and (b) together.
-- Under reading P2 this would be TRUE; the original says FALSE.
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS TRUE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS TRUE
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- (b)'s proviso: the swimming-pool exclusion revives the exclusion
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS TRUE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS TRUE
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- no animal cause: the exclusion list alone does nothing
#EVAL `insurance covered` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS TRUE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- helper: insects count as an animal cause
#EVAL `loss or damage by animals` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS TRUE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- helper: Contents damage without birds is not the carve-out
#EVAL `damage to contents and caused by birds` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS TRUE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- helper: the swimming-pool limb
#EVAL `an exclusion applies` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS TRUE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS TRUE
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- helper: the bare field read
#EVAL `ensuing covered loss` OF
        Inputs
        WITH
            `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS TRUE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
            `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
            `a household appliance` IS FALSE
            `a swimming pool` IS TRUE
            `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
            `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS TRUE
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- the #ASSERT path on the headline decision (boolean shape)
#ASSERT `insurance covered` OF
            Inputs
            WITH
                `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS TRUE
                `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
                `any other exclusion applies` IS FALSE
                `a household appliance` IS FALSE
                `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
                `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> assertion satisfied

-- a second #ASSERT, on a helper
#ASSERT `an exclusion applies` OF
            Inputs
            WITH
                `Loss or Damage.caused by rodents` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.caused by insects` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.caused by vermin` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.caused by birds` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.to Contents` IS FALSE
                `any other exclusion applies` IS TRUE
                `a household appliance` IS FALSE
                `a swimming pool` IS FALSE
                `a plumbing, heating, or air conditioning system` IS FALSE
                `Loss or Damage.ensuing covered loss` IS FALSE
-- L4 oracle ==> assertion satisfied
